(7609885, 1231355, 65234, '<td valign="top">Fabulous detail and just a hint of red. I rather like the softness of the light here.</td>', 'Fabulous detail and just a hint of red. I rather like the softness of the light here.', '2019-01-22 17:56:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7609887, 1231396, 65234, '<td valign="top">VERY red on my phone! Maybe a bit too much, but the detail is great so you still get a great score. My 2nd favorite image in the challenge.</td>', 'VERY red on my phone! Maybe a bit too much, but the detail is great so you still get a great score. My 2nd favorite image in the challenge.', '2019-01-22 17:58:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7609888, 1231343, 65234, '<td valign="top">Very well done!</td>', 'Very well done!', '2019-01-22 17:59:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7609889, 1231351, 65234, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. Maybe a little soft.</td>', 'Very pretty. Maybe a little soft.', '2019-01-22 17:59:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7609894, 1231399, 177030, '<td valign="top">Standard editing?</td>', 'Standard editing?', '2019-01-22 18:09:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7609903, 1231399, 96751, '<td valign="top">This might be one of the best eclipse images ever entered on DPC. I hope you continue to enter challenges. Looking forward to what you can create.</td>', 'This might be one of the best eclipse images ever entered on DPC. I hope you continue to enter challenges. Looking forward to what you can create.', '2019-01-22 20:06:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610313, 1231338, 67258, '<td valign="top">I am really confused by the orientation here - the placement of Tycho and Copernicus craters suggest VERY far South, almost Antarctica.  I wonder if it is from South Island NZ, or the south coast of Australia and tilted when composing or processing?  <br/> <br/>Nonetheless, a fine and interesting moon photo with some clearly definable features.</td>', 'I am really confused by the orientation here - the placement of Tycho and Copernicus craters suggest VERY far South, almost Antarctica.  I wonder if it is from South Island NZ, or the south coast of Australia and tilted when composing or processing?   Nonetheless, a fine and interesting moon photo with some clearly definable features.', '2019-01-25 07:33:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610317, 1231384, 67258, '<td valign="top">Upside down?  Lots of detail here.</td>', 'Upside down?  Lots of detail here.', '2019-01-25 07:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610320, 1231396, 3306, '<td valign="top">My choice for the Blue. One heck of a telephoto lens! Perfect exposure, color, sharpness, size and timing. I like that you can see the stars and there is essentially no noise to be seen. One more element would have made this picture unique.... if you had captured the meteor collision on the surface that was reported in the scientific journals during the eclipse! Is this you Shannon?</td>', 'My choice for the Blue. One heck of a telephoto lens! Perfect exposure, color, sharpness, size and timing. I like that you can see the stars and there is essentially no noise to be seen. One more element would have made this picture unique.... if you had captured the meteor collision on the surface that was reported in the scientific journals during the eclipse! Is this you Shannon?', '2019-01-25 08:14:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610362, 1231343, 24454, '<td valign="top">I really love this!  So creative!</td>', 'I really love this!  So creative!', '2019-01-25 14:19:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610436, 1231397, 3102, '<td valign="top">One of my top 2 picks... excellent stuff!</td>', 'One of my top 2 picks... excellent stuff!', '2019-01-25 22:34:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610604, 1231396, 114285, '<td valign="top">Great Scott! Amazing close up! This is the red, well looks like the blue now because someone got DQ!</td>', 'Great Scott! Amazing close up! This is the red, well looks like the blue now because someone got DQ!', '2019-01-26 21:42:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610605, 1231377, 114285, '<td valign="top">My pick for the the yellow or red.</td>', 'My pick for the the yellow or red.', '2019-01-26 21:42:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610606, 1231309, 114285, '<td valign="top">The yellow ribbon.</td>', 'The yellow ribbon.', '2019-01-26 21:42:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610607, 1231406, 114285, '<td valign="top">Very creative</td>', 'Very creative', '2019-01-26 21:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7610643, 1231396, 67258, '<td valign="top">I think I would prefer this with a bit more space around the moon, but nonetheless, in my top two, and a very fine entry.  Bumping.  Coming back for another view and bumping again - my pick for Blue.  The level of detail and identifiable features is really impressive.  I still would have liked a little more space, and it does seem just a tad over-saturated, but a thoroughly interesting entry.  <br/> <br/>One thing that always amazes me, although I know it and it is quite obvious, is the different view we get from differing latitudes.  For us, Tycho is closer to SW rather than S.</td>', 'I think I would prefer this with a bit more space around the moon, but nonetheless, in my top two, and a very fine entry.  Bumping.  Coming back for another view and bumping again - my pick for Blue.  The level of detail and identifiable features is really impressive.  I still would have liked a little more space, and it does seem just a tad over-saturated, but a thoroughly interesting entry.   One thing that always amazes me, although I know it and it is quite obvious, is the different view we get from differing latitudes.  For us, Tycho is closer to SW rather than S.', '2019-01-27 05:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
